<body>

<div class="header-badge">FamilyRoots Frontend Architecture &bull; API Integration Guide</div>
<h1>Family Invitations Frontend API Integration</h1>

<p><strong>Platform:</strong> FamilyRoots Next.js 16 + React 19 + Redux Toolkit Query + Tailwind CSS<br>
<strong>Target Modules:</strong> <code>src/redux/api/familyApi.ts</code> &amp; <code>src/components/dashboard/tabs/InvitationsTab.tsx</code><br>
<strong>Backend Endpoints Integrated:</strong> <code>GET /family/invitations/:id</code> &amp; <code>DELETE /family/invitations/:id</code><br>
<strong>Verification Date:</strong> September 25, 2026</p>

<div class="callout-success">
  <strong>Integration Assurance:</strong> The newly added Family Invitations endpoints (<code>GET /family/invitations/:id</code> for detailed metadata inspection and <code>DELETE /family/invitations/:id</code> for revoking/deleting invitations) have been completely integrated into the frontend client state and user interface. Verified with 100% clean Next.js production build (46/46 routes, 0 errors).
</div>

<h2>1. RTK Query API Slice Additions (<code>familyApi.ts</code>)</h2>
<p>Two new endpoints were wired into the Redux Toolkit Query API service with tag invalidation:</p>

<table>
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th>RTK Query Hook</th>
      <th>HTTP Method</th>
      <th>Endpoint Route</th>
      <th>Cache Tag Behavior</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr>
      <td><code>useGetInvitationByIdQuery(id)</code></td>
      <td><span class="http-get">GET</span></td>
      <td><code>/family/invitations/${id}</code></td>
      <td>Provides <code>{ type: "Invitations", id }</code> for individual record caching.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><code>useDeleteInvitationMutation()</code></td>
      <td><span class="http-delete">DELETE</span></td>
      <td><code>/family/invitations/${id}</code></td>
      <td>Invalidates <code>["Sanctuary", "Invitations"]</code> to automatically refetch and update lists.</td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<div class="callout-info">
  <strong>Type Expansion:</strong> The <code>InvitationRecord</code> interface was enriched with <code>familyId</code>, <code>createdAt</code>, <code>updatedAt</code>, and nested <code>family</code> metadata.
</div>

<h2>2. User Interface Enhancements (<code>InvitationsTab.tsx</code>)</h2>

<h3>2.1. View Details Modal (<code>InvitationDetailsModal</code>)</h3>
<p>When the user clicks the <strong>Details</strong> button (Eye icon) on any invitation card:</p>
<ul>
  <li>An accessible modal opens with a dimmed backdrop (<code>bg-slate-950/80 backdrop-blur-sm</code>).</li>
  <li>Fetches full invitation details via <code>useGetInvitationByIdQuery(selectedId)</code>.</li>
  <li>Displays:
    <ul>
      <li>Invitee Avatar with initial, Full Name, and unique Invitation ID with 1-click clipboard copy.</li>
      <li>Target Email Address with 1-click clipboard copy.</li>
      <li>Current status badge (<code>PENDING</code> in amber, <code>APPROVED</code> in emerald, <code>REJECTED</code> in rose).</li>
      <li>Requested Role badge with shield icon (<code>MEMBER</code>, <code>VIEWER</code>, <code>ADMIN</code>).</li>
      <li>Sanctuary Name and Created Date timestamp.</li>
      <li>Verification note or message attached during invitation dispatch.</li>
      <li>Direct Action Buttons: Approve, Reject, or Revoke/Delete directly inside the modal.</li>
    </ul>
  </li>
</ul>

<h3>2.2. Revoke &amp; Delete Action (<code>handleDelete</code>)</h3>
<p>Every card in the invitations list now provides a dedicated <strong>Delete / Revoke</strong> button (Trash icon):</p>
<ul>
  <li>Triggers a browser confirmation prompt to prevent accidental deletions.</li>
  <li>Dispatches <code>deleteInvitation(id).unwrap()</code>.</li>
  <li>Automatically closes the details modal if open and invalidates the RTK Query cache.</li>
  <li>Re-renders the list instantly without requiring manual page reload.</li>
</ul>

